 "simulatorGaps": [
  "Naive player (CI bands, L3, this file's main batch): only Vica, the story's own companion; no recruited companions. Competent: recruits and seats companions, but no party combos, duo techniques, dexterity order or hunt-the-healer retarget (sim_combat.dart header).",
  "No Quick Resolve, no momentum surge; no Luck nudges, no Hammersmith die work; a die rerolled only on an empty face (naive).",
  "No battlefield conditions, no chapter threat on enemies, no sellsword; the story walk rolls no encounter affixes and no Elites.",
  "Signs without momentum or the party share; no Titan's Blood; perks without rerolls, momentum or party.",
  "A lost encounter is not a death: after 3 failed tries the walk moves on with health and mana refilled; a lost fight gives no XP. Permadeath is not played (this file derives \"would die in chapter c\" from the first lost encounter).",
  "Choices along the story graph follow the goal only: random, the most good (favorGood), the most evil (favorEvil) or the most gold (maximizeGold); a player reads the scene and avoids or seeks fights. Ability checks are rolled.",
  "Shops: naive buys the spellbook, 2 potions, the best piece per slot by attack + armor, the sage die for a caster; never wears loot, quest rewards or scene grants. Competent wears the best loadout of all it owns, buys dice and merges skills. Shops at a scene, port, built house or the caravan, at most once a chapter; no revisit from the camp (kept off main, sim-reach-v1.766.md).",
  "Stat picks follow fixed per-profession shares (simBuildShares); skill faces by simSkillScore; potions drunk below 40% health.",
  "Clan offers: naive takes the best gift 75% / its best-standing clan 25%, kept to its main clan; competent the gift that raises its power most.",
  "Not played: the companions' crises, the detour choices, the fall-of-the-seat scene; a seat crisis is played at once at the hub (sim-gaps.md, l3-1.888.0.md).",
  "The thieves' purse is not played; land crossings, road events and hunters are, but road hunters and crisis fights are not counted among encounters."
 ]
}